 ```python
def abbreviate_name(name: str) -> str:
    """
    Generates an abbreviated version of the full name.

    Args:
        name (str): The full name to be abbreviated.

    Returns:
        str: The abbreviated name.
    """
    name_parts = name.split(' ')  # Split the name into parts
    abbreviated_name = ''
    for i in range(len(name_parts)):
        # Append the first letter of each part to the abbreviated name
        abbreviated_name += name_parts[i][0]
        # If it's not the last part, add a dot
        if i < len(name_parts) - 1:
            abbreviated_name += '.'
    return abbreviated_name.upper()

# Example usage
name = "John Smith"
abbreviated = abbreviate_name(name)
print(f"Full name: {name}, Abbreviated: {abbreviated}")
 ```
